{"name":"Surfin’","hex":"#73c0d2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Surfin'","blocks":[{"text":"\"Surfin'\" is a song by American rock band the Beach Boys that was written by Brian Wilson and Mike Love. It was released as the debut single by the Beach Boys on November 27, 1961 on Candix Records and was included on the October 1962 album Surfin' Safari."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/45/Beach_boys_X_label_301.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surfin'"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/50/Dennis_Wilson_1961.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/50/Dennis_Wilson_1961.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Dennis Wilson, a surfer, inspired his brother Brian to write the song.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADennis_Wilson_1961.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/The_Beach_Boys_1961.jpg/500px-The_Beach_Boys_1961.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/The_Beach_Boys_1961.jpg/500px-The_Beach_Boys_1961.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Beach Boys on New Year's Eve 1961, a month after they had acquired instruments and recorded the song. From left: Dennis Wilson, Mike Love, Brian and Carl Wilson, and Al Jardine.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Beach_Boys_1961.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/The_Beach_Boys_1963_Billboard_2.png/500px-The_Beach_Boys_1963_Billboard_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip